menu "Digivice board bring-up"
choice DIGIVICE_BOARD
    prompt "Board profile"
    default DIGIVICE_BOARD_GENERIC_SERIAL
    help
        GenericSerial is the safe default and configures no board GPIOs.
        Select an exact verified board before enabling any peripheral.
config DIGIVICE_BOARD_GENERIC_SERIAL
    bool "GenericSerial (no board GPIOs)"
config DIGIVICE_BOARD_WAVESHARE_146
    bool "Waveshare ESP32-S3-Touch-LCD-1.46 standard glass, SKU29565"
    help
        Asserts verified GPIO7 high early to sustain battery power. Native USB
        command/save reboot operation is verified; peripheral acceptance is
        recorded separately. Never formats storage or changes charging control.
config DIGIVICE_BOARD_HELTEC_UNVERIFIED
    bool "Heltec WiFi LoRa 32 V4 (revision unverified; no board GPIOs)"
endchoice
config DIGIVICE_DISPLAY_TOUCH
    bool "Enable physical SPD2010 display, touch and game screens"
    depends on DIGIVICE_BOARD_WAVESHARE_146
    default n
    help
        Exact SKU29565 QSPI panel and shared-bus touch. The game uses an
        explicitly allocated PSRAM framebuffer and one internal DMA stripe.
        Missing framebuffer/display leaves USB and saves available.
config DIGIVICE_AUDIO_MOTION
    bool "Enable physical speaker cues, raw motion and walking detector"
    depends on DIGIVICE_DISPLAY_TOUCH
    default n
    help
        PCM5101 I2S output and QMI8658 raw acceleration/gyro on the existing
        shared bus. An independent sampler feeds a software cadence detector,
        durable lifetime usage and eligible walking encounters. Optional tilt
        is cosmetic. Real walking accuracy still requires bench acceptance;
        no built-in hardware step-counter register is assumed.
        No microphone or background streaming.
choice DIGIVICE_DISPLAY_ORIENTATION
    prompt "Display and touch orientation"
    depends on DIGIVICE_DISPLAY_TOUCH
    default DIGIVICE_DISPLAY_ORIENTATION_NATIVE
    help
        Rotate pixels in software and apply the matching inverse transform to
        touch. Uses the existing framebuffer and DMA stripe; no panel axis-swap
        command. Keep Native until the mounted case direction is confirmed.
config DIGIVICE_DISPLAY_ORIENTATION_NATIVE
    bool "Native (no rotation)"
config DIGIVICE_DISPLAY_ORIENTATION_CW90
    bool "Clockwise 90 degrees from native"
config DIGIVICE_DISPLAY_ORIENTATION_CCW90
    bool "Counterclockwise 90 degrees from native"
endchoice
config DIGIVICE_SD_ASSETS
    bool "Use microSD as the primary downloaded-asset cache"
    depends on DIGIVICE_BOARD_WAVESHARE_146
    default y
    help
        Mount the existing FAT card using verified one-bit SDMMC wiring and
        one bounded cache file. Never formats a card or repairs a foreign,
        incomplete or corrupt cache automatically. Missing/unwritable cards
        keep the compiled artwork fallback; no internal-flash cache switch.
config DIGIVICE_QMI_PEDOMETER
    bool "Enable legacy read-only QMI8658 counter experiment"
    depends on DIGIVICE_BOARD_WAVESHARE_146
    default n
    help
        Creates the board-owned shared I2C bus on SCL10/SDA11. The QMI adapter
        only reads identity/configuration/counter registers. It never enables
        or calibrates the sensor. Physical steps require a verified revision,
        externally verified sensor configuration and later accuracy testing.
        Leave disabled for the raw-sample software walking detector above.
config DIGIVICE_PRIVATE_SD_ART
    bool "Allow manually supplied private exact-form DVA artwork"
    depends on DIGIVICE_SD_ASSETS
    default n
    help
        Explicit local-use option. Reads one fixed8.3 DSFnnnnn.DVA file for
        the selected form, validates DVA dimensions/CRC and decodes one32px
        frame at a time. These files are unsigned user-selected content;
        provenance stays in the accompanying host export. Does not download
        private art, scan the roster, or enable a physical LCD renderer.
config DIGIVICE_QMI_EXPECTED_REVISION
    int "Bench-verified QMI revision register value (0 = unverified)"
    depends on DIGIVICE_QMI_PEDOMETER
    range 0 255
    default 0
    help
        Do not guess a revision from the family WHO_AM_I value. Zero keeps
        physical counter readings disabled until the actual part is verified.
endmenu

menu "Digivice network development"
config DIGIVICE_ALLOW_PRIVATE_HTTP
    bool "Allow explicitly provisioned private IPv4 HTTP service origins"
    default n
    help
        Development only. Runtime configuration must additionally opt in.
        Only literal RFC1918 IPv4 addresses are accepted; no public HTTP,
        DNS exception, redirects or insecure HTTPS certificate fallback.
        WPA2 Wi-Fi credentials in NVS are not encrypted by this prototype.
config DIGIVICE_DEVELOPMENT_ASSETS
    bool "Accept the public development asset signing key"
    default n
    help
        Development fixtures only. The RFC6979 example signing key is public
        and provides no production authenticity. Enable only for local tests.
        Production signed assets need a private publisher key and a distinct
        firmware trust pin; do not ship this option as a production trust root.
endmenu
